---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Martin Rebo, a senior software engineer focused on TypeScript, cloud systems, and observability."
>
  <section class="page-intro prose-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
    <h1>Senior software engineer with a bias for simple systems that age well.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I work across TypeScript, React, Node.js, and cloud platforms, with particular interest in
      reliability, observability, and designing systems teams can reason about quickly.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        My work sits at the intersection of product delivery and operational quality. I enjoy
        building interfaces that feel fast, APIs that fail predictably, and platform capabilities
        that help teams move with confidence.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is where I publish notes about system design, performance, testing, cloud
        infrastructure, OpenTelemetry, Grafana, and lessons from shipping production software.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care deeply about maintainability: descriptive naming, good defaults, excellent docs, and
        removing complexity before adding abstractions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
